# Got to Get You into My Life, verse (figure 102.1)
# A A B B C: the first system is played twice. In the B phrases the b-minor chord is held in the
# upper voices over a chromatically descending bassline; the last bass note, G#, makes it a
# half-diminished seventh on G# (vii half-dim of ii). The C phrase descends diatonically from C.
#? Bass octave (B2 down to G2) chosen for range.
